  "limitations": [
    "GQL has no free, redistributable conformance suite comparable to the openCypher TCK or the Apache TinkerPop gremlin-test suite. This profile is authored against the GQL grammar vendored at data/language/GQL.g4 and is deliberately smaller than the Cypher profile rather than padded out with Cypher queries renamed to GQL keywords.",
    "The local data/gql_test corpus is not used as a strict oracle: its LDBC rewrites are best-effort and mostly record only the shape of the expected result.",
    "This is a grammar-scoped profile: every scored statement must be expressible by the frozen data/language/GQL.g4. Standard GQL constructs outside that grammar, including STARTS/ENDS/CONTAINS, predicate IN, postfix indexing, and SIZE, require a separate experiment with a repaired or replaced grammar. A perfect score therefore does not establish full ISO GQL conformance."
  ]
